<title>BELGIUM: EU sugar committee to study set-aside yeast plan.</title>
<headline>EU sugar committee to study set-aside yeast plan.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A plan to allow non-sugar crops intended for yeast production to be grown on set-aside land is due to be studied by the European Union's sugar management committee on Wednesday, an EU member state official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The committee will discuss the possible impact on the sugar industry,&quot; the official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Yeast is a by-product of sugar.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committee is due to discuss in May a draft proposal to allow farmers to use set-aside land to grow crops for yeast production.</p>
<p>Under the 1992 reform of the Common Agricultural Policy (CAP) a programme of setting aside land to limit cereals cultivation was introduced to cut excess production.</p>
</text>
